  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given that $(2 \\cos \\theta, 2 \\sin \\theta)$ will lie on the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}=4$ (from the given figure). Since, point lies on the region containing origin.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2015_mat_a136.png\">\r\nSo, point will be on the shaded region.\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$\\theta \\in\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)$",
